    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present No. 106 Thomond Road, Ballyfermot, Dublin 10 to the market. This attractive two-bedroom, one-bathroom terraced property is ideally positioned within a highly sought-after and mature pocket of Ballyfermot and comes to the market in good, clean condition throughout. With the added benefit of an attic conversion and low-maintenance gardens to both the front and rear, this property is sure to appeal to first-time buyers, downsizers and investors alike.\nThomond Road is a well-established residential location, with a host of local amenities and services close by. Ballyfermot village is within easy reach, offering a wide selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday conveniences, while there are numerous schools, recreational facilities and green spaces in the surrounding area. The property also benefits from excellent transport links providing easy access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding suburbs, with the M50 and N4 both readily accessible.\nInternally, the accommodation comprises of a welcoming entrance porch/hall, a bright living room and an extension to the rear featuring a spacious bathroom and kitchen/dining area. Upstairs are two well-proportioned bedroom. The property further benefits from an attic conversion, providing a versatile additional space which could suit a variety of uses, subject to the necessary requirements. Outside, the property boasts low-maintenance front and rear gardens, offering practical outdoor space with minimal upkeep.\nThe property is presented in good, clean condition and offers an excellent opportunity for any buyer looking to acquire a home in a mature and well-established Ballyfermot setting. The combination of its spacious accommodation, attic conversion, manageable gardens and highly convenient location makes No. 106 Thomond Road a property that is well worth viewing.\nFeatures\n•Two-bed/ one bath terraced property\n•BER E\n•C. 70 sqm of internal floorspace\n•Attic conversion suitable for a variety of uses\n•Presented in good, clean condition throughout\n•Low-maintenance front and rear gardens\n•Vacant possession\n•No onward chain\n•Mature and highly sought-after residential location\n•Excellent transport links\n•Ideal for first-time buyers, downsizers or investors\nDirections\nEircode D10 KX21\n"
      },
